{
  "duration": 82.699,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.239,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.68,
      "end": 1.679,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.18,
      "end": 3.299,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.879,
      "end": 4.94,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.339,
      "end": 6.219,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.739,
      "end": 8.319,
      "text": "we have a vertical stick."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.72,
      "end": 9.719,
      "text": "The question says"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.239,
      "end": 13.539,
      "text": "that the shadow of the stick is equal to its height,"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.059,
      "end": 16.859,
      "text": "and we need to find the sun's angle of elevation."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.379,
      "end": 19.959,
      "text": "Let the angle of elevation be theta."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.699,
      "end": 23.0,
      "text": "Before solving, let us quickly understand the picture."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.379,
      "end": 25.399,
      "text": "The stick is standing straight,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.879,
      "end": 28.219,
      "text": "so its height becomes the opposite side."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.619,
      "end": 29.939,
      "text": "The shadow is on the ground,"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.359,
      "end": 32.18,
      "text": "so it becomes the adjacent side."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.579,
      "end": 34.359,
      "text": "That is all we need for this question."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.04,
      "end": 37.5,
      "text": "Since we know the opposite side and the adjacent side,"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.939,
      "end": 42.299,
      "text": "the correct trigonometric ratio to use is ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.919,
      "end": 44.219,
      "text": "So tan theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.939,
      "end": 47.179,
      "text": "is equal to opposite upon adjacent."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.5,
      "end": 49.18,
      "text": "Now let us put the given values."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.7,
      "end": 57.579,
      "text": "The height is equal to the shadow, so tan theta is equal to height upon shadow, which becomes one upon one."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.079,
      "end": 59.619,
      "text": "That means tan theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.939,
      "end": 61.02,
      "text": "is equal to one."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.459,
      "end": 63.699,
      "text": "Now we know one standard trigonometric value."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.26,
      "end": 82.699,
      "text": "Tan forty-five degrees is equal to one. Since tan theta is also equal to one, the value of theta must be forty-five degrees. Got it? Perfect. So the sun's angle of elevation is forty-five degrees. Hence, the correct option is option A, forty-five degrees"
    }
  ],
